title: Oversight and Investigations
subtitle: Hold power to account.
tags: govt_action
new-page: true
view-if: oversight_timer <= 0 and (house_d >= 218 or senate_d >= 51) and white_house == "R"
choose-if: capital >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: We need at least 2 capital.
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; capital -= 2; oversight_timer = 2

= Oversight and Investigations

With a congressional majority, we have subpoena power. Used well, it protects the republic. Used badly, it looks like a partisan show.

- @focused: Focused, factual hearings.
- @blockbuster: Blockbuster hearings with maximum media.
- @impeach: Begin impeachment proceedings.

@focused
subtitle: Slow, credible.
on-arrival: stability += 3; media_trust += 2; enthusiasm += 1; pop_mod += 0.1

Quiet, careful work. The record builds.

@blockbuster
subtitle: Big audience, mixed effect.
on-arrival: enthusiasm += 4; media_trust -= 1; maga += 2; pop_mod += 0.1; stability += 1

Ratings are good. Persuasion is another matter.

@impeach
subtitle: Risky and polarizing, but sometimes necessary.
view-if: maga >= 40
on-arrival: stability += 4; enthusiasm += 6; maga += 4; unity += 3; mod_dissent += 5; pop_mod -= 0.1; far_right += 2

The Constitution gives the House this tool for a reason. Whether to use it is a judgment about the republic, about politics, and about what comes next.
